The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
-  public void reload() {
-    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
-      ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
```
Reason:
The removal of the `reloadText()` method call in the `reload()` function meant that the help text was not being updated when commands were reloaded. This led to the `/help` command displaying outdated or incorrect information, as the mechanism to refresh the help text was eliminated.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
public void reload() {
    for (ServerCommand serverCommand : serverCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) serverCommand).reloadText();
    }
    for (PlayerCommand playerCommand : playerCommands.values()) {
        ((AbstractCommand) playerCommand).reloadText();
    }
}
```
Reason:
Reintroducing the `reloadText()` method calls ensures that the help text for both server and player commands is refreshed whenever the `reload()` method is invoked. This restores the functionality needed to display the correct help information when the `/help` command is executed.

